==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|baldachin}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|baldaquin}}, from {{etyl|it|en}} {{m|it|baldacchino}}, from {{m|it|Baldacca}}, a variant of [[Baghdad]], where the material originally came from.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈbældəkɪn/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{label|en|uncountable|archaic}} A kind of embroidered material with gold thread-work.
# A fine [[canopy]] of [[silk]], erected over [[shrine]]s, thrones, etc.

====Translations====
